title: Header-only Conan recipes need target-profile graph evidence and a real signed consumer launch
scope: Conan2 header-only C++ packages on OpenHarmony PC
trigger: A package exports only public headers and has no dependency closure, but target validation still needs an OHOS profile and executable evidence.
phenomenon: Host Conan create can pass while target package identity and runtime signing remain unproven.
root_cause: Header-only layout removes linker dependencies, not target settings identity or runtime-loader/signature requirements of a consumer.
repair: Use an isolated profile with os.version=6.0, compiler clang15, libc++, cppstd17; run graph info --build=never; cross-compile one consumer for aarch64; transfer exact bytes over the authorized USB-HDC transport; self-sign with the native signer; launch once and read back cleanup.
verification: fast-cpp-csv-parser target graph nodes=1 dependencies=0 info_invalid=null; consumer launch rc=0 and rows=2; process and temporary CSV absent; release/postrelease PASS.
boundary: Graph-only W0 does not replace CI, AI Review, Pre-PR, or submission. A consumed launch cannot be replayed; identity drift requires a new run.
